(399251, 34135, 2000, '<td valign="top">The house is crooked.  I realize that is not correctable in Post-processing, but I think it should have been retaken so the house would be level.</td>', 'The house is crooked.  I realize that is not correctable in Post-processing, but I think it should have been retaken so the house would be level.', '2003-08-25 23:01:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(399252, 34449, 11073, '<td valign="top">nice pic. i like the composition, the dof, and the perspective here. nice work.</td>', 'nice pic. i like the composition, the dof, and the perspective here. nice work.', '2003-08-25 23:02:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(399253, 33916, 2000, '<td valign="top">Nice catch - they are definitely from the past.</td>', 'Nice catch - they are definitely from the past.', '2003-08-25 23:02:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(399257, 34110, 2000, '<td valign="top">Would have worked well for negative space, I think - here, there''s not enough of the truck showing that a person not really familiar with old vehicles would recognize.</td>', 'Would have worked well for negative space, I think - here, there''s not enough of the truck showing that a person not really familiar with old vehicles would recognize.', '2003-08-25 23:03:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(399262, 33406, 2000, '<td valign="top">Given that rotation WAS allowed (per a statement from Langdon in the forums), this should have been rotated by you.  However, since the rules were never changed on the challenge page, I can deal with it.  This really captures an element of the past, and it does so in a very appealing fashion.</td>', 'Given that rotation WAS allowed (per a statement from Langdon in the forums), this should have been rotated by you.  However, since the rules were never changed on the challenge page, I can deal with it.  This really captures an element of the past, and it does so in a very appealing fashion.', '2003-08-25 23:05:26.000000', NULL, 1),
